# Talk2Me Communication Platform Architecture

## Vision

Talk2Me is not a video conferencing application.

Talk2Me is an inclusive communication platform designed to ensure that every participant can communicate effectively regardless of language, hearing ability, speaking ability, literacy level, device capability, or internet quality.

Our goal is to build the most accessible and intelligent meeting experience in the world.

---

# Core Principle

We do not want to rebuild Zoom, Google Meet, or Microsoft Teams.

Instead, we focus on solving communication barriers while leveraging proven real-time communication infrastructure.

The platform must support:

* Video meetings
* Audio meetings
* Chat
* Screen sharing
* AI assistance
* Accessibility features
* Real-time collaboration

---

# Architecture Decision

## Approved Architecture

Talk2Me will use an SFU (Selective Forwarding Unit) architecture powered by LiveKit.

### Why

Building custom WebRTC signaling, media routing, TURN infrastructure, and participant management would significantly increase development complexity while providing little competitive advantage.

Our innovation lies in communication intelligence and accessibility, not in media transport.

### Architecture Overview

User Devices
↓
LiveKit SFU
↓
Talk2Me Services
↓
AI Services
↓
Accessibility Services

---

# Core Infrastructure

## LiveKit

LiveKit will provide:

* Room management
* Video streaming
* Audio streaming
* Screen sharing
* Participant management
* Recording
* Reconnection handling
* TURN/STUN support
* Network optimization

## Cloudflare

Cloudflare will provide:

* API services
* Authentication
* Room creation
* Session management
* AI service orchestration
* Edge deployment

## Database

PostgreSQL will store:

* Users
* Organizations
* Meeting metadata
* Chat history
* Recordings metadata
* AI summaries
* Accessibility preferences

